elease fans wondered whether the real  eddie van halen played the music heard  on the edward van halen cassette tape  speaking in an on-the-fly interview with  tmz in 2012  van halen confirmed that it's true those  are his awesome 80s guitar riffs you  hear in back to the future  the guitar legend never made a big deal  about his contribution to the iconic  film  he called the recording just a bunch of  noise which to be fair  it is but it's still one of those fun  back to the future details  that are hard not to love while he  didn't provide the guitar track for  johnny b  good that was guitarist tim may or kick  in on the songs by huey lewis and the  news  van halen did indeed play a part in  exploding the eardrums of crisping  glover's young george mcfly  and that deserves some serious applause  in its own right eddie van halen wasn't  the only rock star to make a subtle  appearance in back to the future  huey lewis of huey lewis on the news  appears as a judge when marty's group  auditions for his school's battle of the  band's competition  unfortunately huey has some harsh  criticism for the group  i'm afraid then there's flea  the long time basis for the red hot  chili peppers he shows up in both back  to the future sequels  as marty's longtime frenemy needles in a  less subtle cameo  zz top performs drawing part 3 playing  the 1885 hill valley fair  a young elijah wood also appeared as a  kid trying to play an old arcade game in  part 2  but that wouldn't exactly count as a  celebrity easter egg unless you had some  kind of time machine  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  great movie cameos are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one
 

